    "created_at": "2016-04-05T19:02:08Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-04-05T19:02:08Z",
    "body": "I'm not sure what's attempting to be accomplished here.  Requiring CORS-enabled is a _very_ different relationship to requiring integrity.  The former means the resource owner approves hotlinking.  The latter means the resource user is protected against the resource changing underneath them.\n\nWhat purpose did requiring CORS originally serve, such that it can be replaced by requiring integrity and achieve roughly the same goals?\n",
