    "created_at": "2016-04-06T06:08:57Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-04-06T06:08:57Z",
    "body": "@Mardeg per https://w3c.github.io/webappsec-subresource-integrity/#is-response-eligible-for-integrity-validation CORS is a requirement for subresource integrity. Otherwise you can perform the equivalent of a dictionary-attack.\n\nSupporting the integrity attribute on `track` elements should probably go through https://github.com/w3c/webappsec-subresource-integrity first and then upstreamed here. Though note that you won't get a CORS exemption per my comment above. We're (mostly) done poking holes in the same-origin policy.\n\nHope that's sufficient information.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
